    "slug": "best-kitten-food-2026",
    "title": "Best Kitten Food 2026: Growth Calories, DHA, and Weaning Off Queen’s Milk",
    "description": "Best kitten food 2026: growth-approved wet and dry, feeding frequency, DHA, and when to switch toward adult food. Vet-first notes from Petshiwü.",
    "publishedAt": "2026-03-21T10:00:00.000Z",
    "html": "<p>Kittens are not small adult cats. They need more calories per pound, more frequent meals, and a growth-approved nutrient profile. A cute “all ages” can that is adult-only on the back panel is a miss. This 2026 Petshiwü guide covers weaning through the first year and the red flags that are not picky eating.</p>\n<figure>\n  <picture><source srcset=\"/blog/kitten.webp\" type=\"image/webp\" />\n  <img src=\"/blog/kitten.jpg\" alt=\"Kitten eating growth-formula wet food from a shallow saucer during a 2026 kitten-food guide\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" loading=\"eager\" /></picture>\n  <figcaption>Kitten eating growth-formula wet food from a shallow saucer during a 2026 kitten-food guide</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<h2>Growth statement first, texture second</h2>\n<p>Look for AAFCO growth or all-life-stages wording. Kittens often do best on wet food they can lap, with optional kitten kibble as they learn to crunch. DHA is a common add for brain and vision support. It does not replace complete minerals or parasite control.</p>\n<p>Orphan or early-weaned kittens may need a milk replacer designed for kittens — never cow’s milk as the plan. If a kitten is fading, that is urgent veterinary care, not a new can.</p>\n<h2>How often to put food down</h2>\n<p>Young kittens may eat four or more times a day. Free-choice dry can work for some growing kittens if body condition stays lean; wet meals should still be picked up so you notice a skipped bowl. See <a href=\"/learning/how-much-to-feed-a-cat\">feeding math</a> as they approach adult size.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Keep fresh water in a low bowl or fountain.</li>\n<li>Weigh the kitten weekly.</li>\n<li>Do not feed dog food as a shortcut.</li>\n<li>Ask about deworming on the same schedule as vaccines.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>When to switch toward adult food</h2>\n<p>Many cats move toward adult food around 12 months. Large-breed cats and some indoor cats that are already overweight at ten months may need an earlier calorie conversation. Transition over a week. See <a href=\"/learning/best-wet-cat-food-2026\">wet food 2026</a> if you are staying on cans.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/blog/kitten.webp\" alt=\"Kitten eating growth-formula wet food from a shallow saucer during a 2026 kitten-food guide\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<h2>GI and appetite emergencies in kittens</h2>\n<p>Repeated vomiting, silent straining in the litter box, a bloated belly, or a kitten too weak to eat is same-day care. Do not rotate five proteins hoping a flavor fixes panleukopenia or a foreign string.</p>\n<h2>Shopping the first case</h2>\n<p>Pick one complete kitten food you can buy again. Browse <a href=\"/cat\">the cat aisle</a> and keep a shallow dish that does not bump whiskers raw. Pair feeding with <a href=\"/learning/litter-box-training-a-kitten\">litter training</a> so mealtime and box time stay predictable.</p>\n<h2>Shop this at Petshiwü</h2>\n<p>Shop complete kitten foods and shallow dishes at Petshiwü. Free shipping over $49, no autoship. NYC delivery now; nationwide shipping soon.</p>\n<p><a href=\"/cat\">Browse matching products at Petshiwü</a> — free shipping over $49, no autoship.</p>\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Can kittens eat adult cat food?</h3>\n<p>Only if the product is approved for growth or all life stages. Adult-maintenance-only food can undershoot a kitten’s needs. Ask your veterinarian.</p>\n<h3>Is dry kitten food OK?</h3>\n<p>Complete kitten kibble can be part of the plan. Wet food helps moisture and is easier for tiny mouths. Many households mix.</p>\n<h3>How long do I feed kitten food?</h3>\n<p>Often until about 12 months, then transition. Your veterinarian may adjust for body condition or a medical issue.</p>\n<h2>Related Petshiwü guides</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/best-wet-cat-food-2026\">Best Wet Cat Food 2026: Moisture, Complete Pâtés, and Picky Cans</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/how-much-to-feed-a-cat\">How Much to Feed a Cat: Kcal, Body Condition, and the Bottomless Bowl</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/litter-box-training-a-kitten\">Litter Box Training a Kitten: Location, Sides, and the One-Litter Rule</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>This article is educational and is not a diagnosis or treatment plan. Ask your veterinarian before you change food, supplements, or medicine, and seek care right away for blood in stool or vomit, repeated vomiting, trouble breathing, collapse, or a pet that cannot keep water down.</em></p>",
