    "title": "Best Senior Cat Food: Protein, Phosphorus, and the 11-Year Check",
    "description": "Best senior cat food: when to switch, why many seniors still need protein, phosphorus caveats, and how dental pain masquerades as pickiness. Ask your vet.",
    "publishedAt": "2026-03-24T11:00:00.000Z",
    "html": "<p>Cats hide illness, then get called picky. A senior formula can help if it matches real labs and real teeth. It can harm if you slashed protein because a bag said 11+ and the kidneys were never checked. This Petshiwü guide is educational. Bloodwork and a dental look belong to your veterinarian.</p>\n<figure>\n  <picture><source srcset=\"/blog/senior-cat.webp\" type=\"image/webp\" />\n  <img src=\"/blog/senior-cat.jpg\" alt=\"Older cat with a raised wet-food dish and a senior wellness checklist in the background\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" loading=\"eager\" /></picture>\n  <figcaption>Older cat with a raised wet-food dish and a senior wellness checklist in the background</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<h2>Do not guess at kidneys from the birthday</h2>\n<p>Many senior bags lower phosphorus and calories. That can be appropriate after a diagnosis. It is a poor default for a muscled 12-year-old with normal labs. Unexplained weight loss, more water in the bowl, or peeing outside the box are clinic signs. See <a href=\"/learning/best-cat-food-for-kidney-support\">kidney support</a> for how prescription diets differ from grocery senior cans.</p>\n<p>Healthy seniors often need enough protein to protect muscle. Ask for a senior panel before you “put them on senior.”</p>\n<h2>Texture is half the senior bowl</h2>\n<p>Missing teeth and sore mouths make dry food a bluff. Warm pâté, smaller meals, and a wide dish help. If the cat sniffs and leaves, think nausea or pain before you think snobbery. See <a href=\"/learning/picky-cat-not-eating\">picky cat not eating</a>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Weigh the cat every two weeks after a switch.</li>\n<li>Count treats — tuna juice is not free.</li>\n<li>Keep a fountain; seniors still dehydrate — <a href=\"/learning/cat-water-fountain-benefits\">fountains</a>.</li>\n<li>Ask before adding fish-oil or phosphate binders on your own.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Hyperthyroidism and diabetes change the menu</h2>\n<p>A skinny senior with a huge appetite is not a success story until the clinic rules out hyperthyroidism. A fat senior with extra thirst may be diabetic. Food is part of those plans only after diagnosis. This article will not pick a prescription for you.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/blog/senior-cat.webp\" alt=\"Older cat with a raised wet-food dish and a senior wellness checklist in the background\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<h2>Indoor senior extras</h2>\n<p>Joint stiffness and litter-box avoidance often travel together. A lower-sided box and a nearby meal station can matter more than a new slogan. Pair food with <a href=\"/learning/best-cat-food-for-indoor-cats\">indoor feeding</a> if calories crept up over years of free-fed kibble.</p>\n<h2>Shopping after the appointment</h2>\n<p>Bring the current can to the vet. Then shop the complete food they agree with in <a href=\"/cat\">our cat aisle</a>. Transition slowly unless they want a faster medical change.</p>\n<h2>Shop this at Petshiwü</h2>\n<p>Find senior-complete cat foods and easy-to-lap pâtés at Petshiwü. Free shipping over $49, no autoship. NYC delivery now; nationwide shipping soon.</p>\n<p><a href=\"/cat\">Browse matching products at Petshiwü</a> — free shipping over $49, no autoship.</p>\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>At what age should a cat eat senior food?</h3>\n<p>There is no single age. Use labs, body condition, and dental comfort. Some cats stay on adult food with a smaller portion.</p>\n<h3>Do senior cats need less protein?</h3>\n<p>Not automatically. Muscle loss is common in older cats. Reduced protein is a veterinary decision, often tied to diagnosed kidney disease.</p>\n<h3>Is wet food better for senior cats?</h3>\n<p>Often, because of moisture and chew comfort. It still must be complete and calorie-appropriate.</p>\n<h2>Related Petshiwü guides</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/best-cat-food-for-kidney-support\">Best Cat Food for Kidney Support: Prescription Diets and What OTC Cannot Do</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/best-wet-cat-food-2026\">Best Wet Cat Food 2026: Moisture, Complete Pâtés, and Picky Cans</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/how-much-to-feed-a-cat\">How Much to Feed a Cat: Kcal, Body Condition, and the Bottomless Bowl</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>This article is educational and is not a diagnosis or treatment plan. Ask your veterinarian before you change food, supplements, or medicine, and seek care right away for blood in stool or vomit, repeated vomiting, trouble breathing, collapse, or a pet that cannot keep water down.</em></p>",
