    "slug": "raw-cat-food-safety",
    "title": "Raw Cat Food Safety: Pathogens, Completeness, and High-Risk Homes",
    "description": "Raw cat food safety: Salmonella risk, complete commercial raw vs DIY, kitchen hygiene, and which households should skip raw entirely. Vet-first guidance.",
    "publishedAt": "2026-04-02T08:00:00.000Z",
    "html": "<p>Cats eat prey in nature. Your kitchen is not nature, and your sink is connected to a person who touches a phone. Raw cat food can be commercially complete, and it can also shed Salmonella onto a counter a toddler uses. This Petshiwü safety guide is for people who want the risks in daylight before they thaw the first patty.</p>\n<figure>\n  <picture><source srcset=\"/blog/wet-cat-food.webp\" type=\"image/webp\" />\n  <img src=\"/blog/wet-cat-food.jpg\" alt=\"Frozen raw cat-food patties on a sanitized tray with a separate cutting board for safe handling\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" loading=\"eager\" /></picture>\n  <figcaption>Frozen raw cat-food patties on a sanitized tray with a separate cutting board for safe handling</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<h2>Commercial complete raw versus a chopped chicken breast</h2>\n<p>A formulated raw diet includes calcium, taurine, and vitamins in a planned range. A grocery chicken breast is not a cat diet. DIY raw is a common way cats develop taurine-related heart disease and bone problems. If you still want raw-style nutrition with less freezer drama, some freeze-dried complete foods exist — handle them like raw if the label says raw.</p>\n<p>High-pressure processing reduces some pathogens; it is not a magic sterilizer. Read the manufacturer’s safety statement.</p>\n<h2>People get sick from pet food too</h2>\n<p>Households with young children, pregnant people, older adults, or immunocompromised members should ask a veterinarian before feeding raw. Cats walk on counters. They groom paws that stood in a raw bowl. Wash bowls in hot soapy water. Keep raw packs away from human produce.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator, not on the counter.</li>\n<li>Discard leftovers on the brand’s schedule.</li>\n<li>Do not let raw juices drip into the kibble bin.</li>\n<li>Wash hands before you touch a baby or a laptop.</li>\n<li>Keep the cat’s raw diet away from the dog if the dog is a counter-surfer.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Who should not start raw</h2>\n<p>Cats on immunosuppressive drugs, cats with pancreatitis history, and cats that live with high-risk people are poor DIY raw candidates. Cats already on a prescription urinary or renal diet should not be “upgraded” to raw without the prescribing veterinarian.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/blog/wet-cat-food.webp\" alt=\"Frozen raw cat-food patties on a sanitized tray with a separate cutting board for safe handling\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<h2>A calmer moisture alternative</h2>\n<p>If your goal is moisture and aroma, a complete wet food often gets you there with a cooked kill step. See <a href=\"/learning/best-wet-cat-food-2026\">wet food 2026</a>. That is not anti-raw morality. It is risk matching.</p>\n<h2>If you still choose commercial raw</h2>\n<p>Transition slowly, keep lot codes, and watch stool. Shop complete foods in <a href=\"/cat\">the cat aisle</a>. Call the clinic for blood in stool, vomiting, or a cat that hides and will not eat.</p>\n<h2>Shop this at Petshiwü</h2>\n<p>Shop complete commercial cat foods at Petshiwü. Free shipping over $49, no autoship. NYC delivery now; nationwide shipping soon. Ask your veterinarian before raw.</p>\n<p><a href=\"/cat\">Browse matching products at Petshiwü</a> — free shipping over $49, no autoship.</p>\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Is raw cat food safe?</h3>\n<p>It can be fed more safely as a complete commercial product with strict hygiene. It is never zero-risk. High-risk homes should usually skip it.</p>\n<h3>Does raw food clean cats’ teeth?</h3>\n<p>Chewing meat is not a dental cleaning. Cats still need home care and veterinary oral exams. See our cat dental guide.</p>\n<h3>Can I feed raw eggs or raw fish daily?</h3>\n<p>Do not invent extras. Raw fish can interfere with thiamine. Completeness comes from the formulated product, not a garnish pile.</p>\n<h2>Related Petshiwü guides</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/best-wet-cat-food-2026\">Best Wet Cat Food 2026: Moisture, Complete Pâtés, and Picky Cans</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/homemade-dog-food-safety\">Homemade Dog Food Safety: Why Turkey-and-Rice Is Not a Diet</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/best-raw-dog-food-for-beginners\">Best Raw Dog Food for Beginners: A Safety-First Starter Plan</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>This article is educational and is not a diagnosis or treatment plan. Ask your veterinarian before you change food, supplements, or medicine, and seek care right away for blood in stool or vomit, repeated vomiting, trouble breathing, collapse, or a pet that cannot keep water down.</em></p>",
