    "description": "Cat UTI symptoms: frequent box trips, blood, crying, and why a blocked male cat cannot wait. Educational only — this is not a diagnosis or a home protocol.",
    "publishedAt": "2026-05-01T13:00:00.000Z",
    "html": "<p>Cats do not send a text that they have a urinary problem. They visit the box, produce a bead of urine, or pee on the sink. In males, a blockage can be fatal within hours. This Petshiwü page is recognition and urgency — not a cranberry protocol.</p>\n<figure>\n  <picture><source srcset=\"/blog/cat-litter.webp\" type=\"image/webp\" />\n  <img src=\"/blog/cat-litter.jpg\" alt=\"Cat in a litter box with a small urine clump, illustrating straining and urinary warning signs\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" loading=\"eager\" /></picture>\n  <figcaption>Cat in a litter box with a small urine clump, illustrating straining and urinary warning signs</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<h2>Signs that mean you call today</h2>\n<p>Frequent trips, crying in the box, licking the penis or vulva, blood-tinged urine, and peeing outside the box are all veterinary signs. A male cat that strains with little or no urine, hides, or has a firm painful belly needs emergency care now. Do not wait to see if a new litter helps.</p>\n<p>Not every “UTI” is infection. Feline idiopathic cystitis is often sterile inflammation. Stones and crystals are another path. Only a clinic can sort them. See <a href=\"/learning/best-cat-food-for-urinary-health\">urinary food</a> after the cat can pee.</p>\n<h2>What you should not do at home</h2>\n<p>Do not squeeze the bladder. Do not give leftover antibiotics. Do not offer cranberry chews as treatment. Do not bathe the cat instead of driving. Keep the box scooped so you can see clump size — see <a href=\"/learning/best-cat-litter-2026\">litter</a>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Note last seen normal urination time.</li>\n<li>Bring a urine sample only if you can catch it without delaying care.</li>\n<li>List any new food, guests, or box changes.</li>\n<li>If you have two cats, say so — the sample might not be from the sick one.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Stress and the apartment box</h2>\n<p>Dirty boxes, one box for three cats, and construction noise can trigger cystitis flares. Add boxes and a fountain — <a href=\"/learning/cat-water-fountain-benefits\">fountains</a> — as support after medical care, not instead of it.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/blog/cat-litter.webp\" alt=\"Cat in a litter box with a small urine clump, illustrating straining and urinary warning signs\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<h2>After the ER</h2>\n<p>Follow the pain medication and diet the veterinarian prescribed. A grocery “urinary care” bag is not automatically the same. Recheck appointments exist because blockages recur.</p>\n<h2>Shopping support products, not treatments</h2>\n<p>Fountains, extra boxes, and complete wet food live in <a href=\"/cat\">the cat aisle</a>. Prescription diets come from the clinic.</p>\n<h2>Shop this at Petshiwü</h2>\n<p>Ready to restock after reading about cat uti symptoms? Petshiwü ships as a nationwide online pet store with free shipping over $49 and no autoship. NYC delivery is available now; nationwide shipping opens soon.</p>\n<p><a href=\"/cat\">Browse matching products at Petshiwü</a> — free shipping over $49, no autoship.</p>\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Can a cat UTI go away on its own?</h3>\n<p>Do not wait to find out, especially with a male cat. Pain and blockage are emergencies. Some cystitis cases are self-limiting, but you cannot tell from the couch.</p>\n<h3>Why is my cat peeing on the bed?</h3>\n<p>Pain, box aversion, and marking are different problems. Rule out medical causes first.</p>\n<h3>Does dry food cause UTIs?</h3>\n<p>Low moisture can contribute to concentrated urine in some cats. It is not the only factor. Format changes happen after the exam.</p>\n<h2>Related Petshiwü guides</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/best-cat-food-for-urinary-health\">Best Cat Food for Urinary Health: Moisture First, Prescription Second</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/best-cat-litter-2026\">Best Cat Litter 2026: Clump, Dust, and the Two-Box Rule</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/cat-water-fountain-benefits\">Cat Water Fountain Benefits: Why Running Water Beats a Stale Bowl</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>This article is educational and is not a diagnosis or treatment plan. Ask your veterinarian before you change food, supplements, or medicine, and seek care right away for blood in stool or vomit, repeated vomiting, trouble breathing, collapse, or a pet that cannot keep water down.</em></p>",
