    "slug": "dog-separation-anxiety-help",
    "title": "Dog Separation Anxiety Help: Panic Versus Boredom and a Real Exit Plan",
    "description": "Dog separation anxiety help: panic vs boredom, crate-exit drills, enrichment, and when to call a veterinary behaviorist. Educational, not a diagnosis.",
    "publishedAt": "2026-05-11T10:00:00.000Z",
    "html": "<p>Separation anxiety is a panic disorder, not a dog being spiteful. Boredom looks similar on a chewed couch and feels different to the dog. This Petshiwü guide helps you sort the two, start safer departures, and know when medication and a behaviorist belong in the plan. We cannot diagnose your dog from a paragraph.</p>\n<figure>\n  <picture><source srcset=\"/blog/dog-anxiety.webp\" type=\"image/webp\" />\n  <img src=\"/blog/dog-anxiety.jpg\" alt=\"Dog watching a door from a prepared crate with a stuffed toy, illustrating a calm departure drill\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" loading=\"eager\" /></picture>\n  <figcaption>Dog watching a door from a prepared crate with a stuffed toy, illustrating a calm departure drill</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<h2>Panic has a signature</h2>\n<p>True separation distress often starts at departure cues: keys, shoes, the elevator chime. Dogs may drool, howl the entire absence, eliminate despite being house-trained, or injure themselves on the door. A dog that sleeps three hours and then shreds a pillow out of boredom is a different project — more exercise and <a href=\"/learning/best-puzzle-toys-for-dogs\">puzzle toys</a>.</p>\n<p>Video the first 20 minutes alone. That clip is what a veterinary behaviorist wants. Neighbors yelling “quiet” is not a treatment.</p>\n<h2>Do not use the crate as a panic chamber</h2>\n<p>If the dog demolishes the crate or breaks teeth on bars, the crate is not the fix today. See <a href=\"/learning/crate-training-an-adult-dog\">adult crate training</a> only if the crate is already a rest place. For panic, you need graduated absences that stay under the threshold where panic starts — often seconds at first.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Practice picking up keys and sitting back down.</li>\n<li>Feed a stuffed <a href=\"/learning/lick-mat-benefits-for-dogs\">lick mat</a> as you step out and right back in.</li>\n<li>Avoid marathon goodbyes.</li>\n<li>If the dog is injuring itself, call the veterinarian the same day.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Medication is not giving up</h2>\n<p>Some dogs need anti-anxiety medication to learn. That decision is medical. CBD is not a validated replacement — see <a href=\"/learning/cbd-for-dogs-what-to-know\">CBD for dogs</a>. Do not stack human Xanax from your cabinet.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/blog/dog-anxiety.webp\" alt=\"Dog watching a door from a prepared crate with a stuffed toy, illustrating a calm departure drill\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<h2>Barking when left is not always SA</h2>\n<p>Alert barking, boredom barking, and panic howling get different plans. See <a href=\"/learning/how-to-stop-dog-barking\">barking</a>. A trainer who only sells shock collars is the wrong hire for panic.</p>\n<h2>Shopping support, not a cure-in-a-box</h2>\n<p>Cameras, puzzle feeders, and a properly sized crate live in <a href=\"/dog\">the dog aisle</a>. The behavior plan lives with professionals.</p>\n<h2>Shop this at Petshiwü</h2>\n<p>Skip the subscription trap and shop dog separation anxiety help gear at Petshiwü. Free shipping over $49, no autoship. NYC delivery is available now; nationwide shipping opens soon.</p>\n<p><a href=\"/dog\">Browse matching products at Petshiwü</a> — free shipping over $49, no autoship.</p>\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Can I just get a second dog?</h3>\n<p>A second dog does not treat separation anxiety and can double the welfare problem. Fix the panic plan first.</p>\n<h3>Is crate training the same as treating SA?</h3>\n<p>No. A crate can be a tool if it is already relaxing. For a panicked dog it can worsen the experience.</p>\n<h3>How long does training take?</h3>\n<p>Weeks to months, with tiny absences at first. Anyone promising a two-day cure is selling something else.</p>\n<h2>Related Petshiwü guides</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/crate-training-an-adult-dog\">Crate Training an Adult Dog: Repairing a Bad History Without Forcing the Door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/how-to-stop-dog-barking\">How to Stop Dog Barking: Name the Job, Then Change the Payoff</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/lick-mat-benefits-for-dogs\">Lick Mat Benefits for Dogs: Calm, Baths, and a Frozen Job for the Mouth</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>This article is educational and is not a diagnosis or treatment plan. Ask your veterinarian before you change food, supplements, or medicine, and seek care right away for blood in stool or vomit, repeated vomiting, trouble breathing, collapse, or a pet that cannot keep water down.</em></p>",
