    "slug": "how-to-reduce-cat-shedding",
    "title": "How to Reduce Cat Shedding: Brushing, Humidity, and Diet Honesty",
    "description": "How to reduce cat shedding: brush types by coat, why indoor heat worsens tumbleweeds, and when sudden hair loss is a veterinary problem, not a vacuum problem.",
    "publishedAt": "2026-06-02T12:00:00.000Z",
    "html": "<p>Cats shed on a cycle and on a thermostat. You will not get to zero fur. You can get to less vomit, fewer tumbleweeds, and earlier notice of bald patches. This Petshiwü guide is brushing technique, indoor humidity, and the medical sheds that a lint roller cannot fix.</p>\n<figure>\n  <picture><source srcset=\"/blog/indoor-cat.webp\" type=\"image/webp\" />\n  <img src=\"/blog/indoor-cat.jpg\" alt=\"Cat being brushed with a steel comb over a towel, showing collected seasonal shed\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" loading=\"eager\" /></picture>\n  <figcaption>Cat being brushed with a steel comb over a towel, showing collected seasonal shed</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<h2>Match the tool to the coat</h2>\n<p>Shorthaired cats often do well with a rubber curry or a fine comb. Longhairs need a steel comb that reaches the skin without ripping mats. Start at the ends of a mat; do not yank a dread toward the skin. If the cat is a wrestler, do two minutes and pay well.</p>\n<p>A lion cut is a last resort for severe matting, done by a professional. Home scissors next to skin are how we see ER lacerations.</p>\n<h2>Heat, daylight, and indoor living</h2>\n<p>Indoor cats can shed year-round because lights and heat confuse seasons. A little humidity helps static and skin. Daily brushing during a blowout beats a monthly marathon. Pair with <a href=\"/learning/best-cat-food-for-hairballs\">hairball food</a> if vomited hair is the complaint.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Brush before play so the session ends on a win.</li>\n<li>Wipe furniture with a damp rubber glove.</li>\n<li>If the cat overgrooms the belly, think itch or pain — not vanity.</li>\n<li>Keep flea prevention current; flea itch looks like shedding.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Diet is completeness, not a magic oil</h2>\n<p>A complete food with adequate fat and protein supports the coat. Dumping fish oil without a plan can upset the gut. Ask your veterinarian before you add oils. Indoor calorie control still matters — see <a href=\"/learning/best-cat-food-for-indoor-cats\">indoor food</a>.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/blog/indoor-cat.webp\" alt=\"Cat being brushed with a steel comb over a towel, showing collected seasonal shed\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<h2>When shedding is disease</h2>\n<p>Symmetric hair loss, scabs, and a moth-eaten coat can be allergy, mites, ringworm, or endocrine disease. Ringworm is contagious to people. Book the clinic instead of buying a third brush.</p>\n<h2>Shopping a two-tool kit</h2>\n<p>Comb plus a rubber brush. Browse <a href=\"/cat\">the cat aisle</a>.</p>\n<h2>Shop this at Petshiwü</h2>\n<p>Petshiwü can send the bowls, foods, and extras this how to reduce cat shedding article points to. Free shipping over $49 and no autoship. NYC delivery is available now; nationwide shipping opens soon.</p>\n<p><a href=\"/cat\">Browse matching products at Petshiwü</a> — free shipping over $49, no autoship.</p>\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>How often should I brush my cat?</h3>\n<p>Shorthairs: a few times a week. Longhairs: daily is kinder than a monthly detangle war.</p>\n<h3>Does a raw diet stop shedding?</h3>\n<p>No honest diet stops normal shed. Completeness and parasite control matter. See our raw-safety article before you change food.</p>\n<h3>Why is there more hair in spring?</h3>\n<p>Many cats blow coat as daylight changes. Increase brushing. Sudden bald spots are still a vet question.</p>\n<h2>Related Petshiwü guides</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/best-cat-food-for-hairballs\">Best Cat Food for Hairball Control: Fiber, Brushing, and When Vomiting Is Not Hair</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/best-cat-food-for-indoor-cats\">Best Cat Food for Indoor Cats: Calories, Boredom, and Hairball Reality</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/how-to-deshed-a-dog\">How to Deshed a Dog: Tools, Timing, and Why Shaving a Double Coat Backfires</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>This article is educational and is not a diagnosis or treatment plan. Ask your veterinarian before you change food, supplements, or medicine, and seek care right away for blood in stool or vomit, repeated vomiting, trouble breathing, collapse, or a pet that cannot keep water down.</em></p>",
