    "html": "<p>Orthopedic is a foam story. If the dog’s hip still hits the floor, it is a pillow with a medical adjective. This Petshiwü guide is thickness, density, and washability for dogs with arthritis — plus the reminder that a bed does not replace a pain exam. See <a href=\"/learning/best-dog-beds-2026\">dog beds 2026</a> for general sizing.</p>\n<figure>\n  <picture><source srcset=\"/blog/dog-bed.webp\" type=\"image/webp\" />\n  <img src=\"/blog/dog-bed.jpg\" alt=\"Large senior dog stretched on a thick foam orthopedic bed with a zip-off washable cover\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" loading=\"eager\" /></picture>\n  <figcaption>Large senior dog stretched on a thick foam orthopedic bed with a zip-off washable cover</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<h2>Foam that does not pancake</h2>\n<p>Look for a stated foam thickness — often 3–5 inches for large dogs — and a density the brand will discuss. Egg-crate toppers feel nice and compress fast under a 90-pound body. Memory foam should rebound slowly, not feel like a camping pad.</p>\n<p>A waterproof liner under a washable cover saves the foam from urine and drool. Zippers should not be a chew toy.</p>\n<h2>Get the dog on and off safely</h2>\n<p>Low-entry beds help seniors. Bolsters can block a stiff dog from stepping in. Place the bed away from slick hardwood or add a rug. Weight loss helps joints more than foam — <a href=\"/learning/how-to-help-an-overweight-dog\">overweight dogs</a>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Measure the sleep stretch, not just the standing length.</li>\n<li>If the dog circles and leaves, the bed may be too small or too tall.</li>\n<li>Give a choice: orthopedic plus a familiar old blanket on top at first.</li>\n<li>Call the vet for new nighttime panting or crying — that is pain, not a picky sleeper.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Supplements and beds are teammates</h2>\n<p>A chew does not replace a mattress, and a mattress does not replace an NSAID when prescribed. See <a href=\"/learning/best-joint-supplements-for-dogs\">joint supplements</a>.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/blog/dog-bed.webp\" alt=\"Large senior dog stretched on a thick foam orthopedic bed with a zip-off washable cover\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<h2>Chewers and orthopedic beds</h2>\n<p>Shredded memory foam is a surgical emergency. Use a cot or a covered bed you supervise until chewing is trained.</p>\n<h2>Shopping a bed that survives year two</h2>\n<p>Thickness, liner, cover. Browse <a href=\"/dog\">the dog aisle</a>.</p>\n<h2>Shop this at Petshiwü</h2>\n<p>When you are ready to put this best orthopedic dog bed article into the cart, Petshiwü is a nationwide online pet store with free shipping over $49 and no autoship. NYC delivery is available now; nationwide shipping opens soon.</p>\n<p><a href=\"/dog\">Browse matching products at Petshiwü</a> — free shipping over $49, no autoship.</p>\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Do orthopedic beds work?</h3>\n<p>They can reduce pressure on joints on hard floors. They do not heal dysplasia. Pair with veterinary pain control and weight management.</p>\n<h3>Can a puppy use an orthopedic bed?</h3>\n<p>Yes, if they will not eat it. Puppies need washable covers more than medical foam.</p>\n<h3>How do I clean memory foam?</h3>\n<p>Usually you do not wash the foam. Wash the cover, wipe the liner, and air the foam if the brand allows. Follow the tag.</p>\n<h2>Related Petshiwü guides</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/best-dog-beds-2026\">Best Dog Beds 2026: Fill, Covers, and a Size That Fits the Curl</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/best-joint-supplements-for-dogs\">Best Joint Supplements for Dogs: What Labels Can Promise and What They Cannot</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/how-to-help-an-overweight-dog\">How to Help an Overweight Dog: Walks, Portions, and Joints That Cannot Wait</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>This article is educational and is not a diagnosis or treatment plan. Ask your veterinarian before you change food, supplements, or medicine, and seek care right away for blood in stool or vomit, repeated vomiting, trouble breathing, collapse, or a pet that cannot keep water down.</em></p>",
