    "description": "Best automatic dog feeder: how to set grams not “cups,” backup batteries, camera extras, and why a feeder is not a substitute for body-condition checks.",
    "publishedAt": "2026-07-15T09:00:00.000Z",
    "html": "<p>An automatic feeder is a clock with a hopper. It shines for shift workers and measured meals. It fails when “one portion” is an uncalibrated cup and a second dog raids the bowl. This Petshiwü buyer’s note is grams, power, and the jobs a feeder cannot do — like notice a dog who stopped eating.</p>\n<figure>\n  <picture><source srcset=\"/blog/kibble-bowl.webp\" type=\"image/webp\" />\n  <img src=\"/blog/kibble-bowl.jpg\" alt=\"Timed automatic dog feeder dispensing a weighed kibble portion into a bowl\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" loading=\"eager\" /></picture>\n  <figcaption>Timed automatic dog feeder dispensing a weighed kibble portion into a bowl</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<h2>Calibrate like a grocer</h2>\n<p>Weigh what the machine actually drops. Hopper “cup” settings lie. Set the daily total from <a href=\"/learning/how-much-to-feed-a-dog\">feeding math</a>, then split meals. If you use a weight-loss food, the feeder still needs the new grams.</p>\n<p>Wet food feeders exist and need stricter cleaning. Most hoppers are for dry food only. Do not leave fresh food in a room-temp carousel unless the product is designed for it.</p>\n<h2>Power and Wi-Fi are not magic</h2>\n<p>A battery backup matters when the outage hits at dinner. Apps that film the bowl are cute and still miss a dog who ate then vomited. If the app fails, the mechanical timer should still drop food.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Keep a lid the dog cannot open.</li>\n<li>In two-dog homes, use a gate or a microchip feeder so portions stay personal.</li>\n<li>Clean the hopper so fat does not go rancid.</li>\n<li>If the dog is suddenly leaving kibble, look at the dog, not the app — <a href=\"/learning/best-dog-food-for-picky-eaters\">picky eaters</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>A slow feeder bowl can sit under the chute</h2>\n<p>Gulpers still gulp from a timed drop. Pair with a <a href=\"/learning/slow-feeder-bowl-benefits\">slow feeder</a> if the machine dumps a pile.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/blog/kibble-bowl.webp\" alt=\"Timed automatic dog feeder dispensing a weighed kibble portion into a bowl\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<h2>What not to outsource</h2>\n<p>Medication, raw food safety, and a puppy’s potty schedule. A feeder does not walk the dog. It does not replace you if the hopper jams while you are away for a weekend.</p>\n<h2>Shopping a hopper you trust</h2>\n<p>Simple timer plus backup power beats a fragile gadget. Browse <a href=\"/dog\">the dog aisle</a>.</p>\n<h2>Shop this at Petshiwü</h2>\n<p>Petshiwü stocks everyday supplies that pair with best automatic dog feeder, without an autoship contract. Free shipping over $49. NYC delivery is available now, and nationwide shipping opens soon — start in our dog collection.</p>\n<p><a href=\"/dog\">Browse matching products at Petshiwü</a> — free shipping over $49, no autoship.</p>\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Are automatic feeders good for picky dogs?</h3>\n<p>They can remove the all-day buffet. They cannot fix nausea. If food sits, call the vet.</p>\n<h3>Can I use one feeder for two dogs?</h3>\n<p>Only with a real separation plan. Free access means the fast eater wins.</p>\n<h3>Do I still need to weigh my dog?</h3>\n<p>Yes. Feeders drift, treats happen, and bodies change. Recheck every two weeks.</p>\n<h2>Related Petshiwü guides</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/how-much-to-feed-a-dog\">How Much to Feed a Dog: Calories, Body Condition, and the Lying Cup</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/slow-feeder-bowl-benefits\">Slow Feeder Bowl Benefits: Gulping, Gas, and a Maze That Is Not Frustrating</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/best-dog-food-for-picky-eaters\">Best Dog Food for Picky Eaters: Aroma, Routine, and Medical Rule-Outs</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>This article is educational and is not a diagnosis or treatment plan. Ask your veterinarian before you change food, supplements, or medicine, and seek care right away for blood in stool or vomit, repeated vomiting, trouble breathing, collapse, or a pet that cannot keep water down.</em></p>",
