    "publishedAt": "2026-07-25T13:00:00.000Z",
    "html": "<p>A snuffle mat is fleece strips on a rubber base where you hide kibble. It turns dinner into a forage. Tired noses are often quieter dogs. This Petshiwü guide is how to start, how to wash the fleece, and when a shredder should not own one unsupervised.</p>\n<figure>\n  <picture><source srcset=\"/blog/dog-toys.webp\" type=\"image/webp\" />\n  <img src=\"/blog/dog-toys.jpg\" alt=\"Dog sniffing kibble hidden in a fleece snuffle mat on the floor\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" loading=\"eager\" /></picture>\n  <figcaption>Dog sniffing kibble hidden in a fleece snuffle mat on the floor</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<h2>Forage is the point</h2>\n<p>Scatter kibble on top first so the dog wins immediately. Then tuck pieces deeper. Use part of the daily ration — <a href=\"/learning/how-much-to-feed-a-dog\">feeding math</a>. A five-minute snuffle can take the edge off a rainy afternoon better than a second walk you do not have time for.</p>\n<p>If the dog rips the fleece out, you have a chewer, not a snuffler. Switch to a rubber puzzle or supervise tightly — <a href=\"/learning/best-toys-for-aggressive-chewers\">chewer toys</a>.</p>\n<h2>Difficulty without cruelty</h2>\n<p>Fold the mat. Use smaller bits. Hide in only one corner. Do not bury food so deep the dog gives up. Pair with other enrichment — <a href=\"/learning/best-puzzle-toys-for-dogs\">puzzles</a> and <a href=\"/learning/lick-mat-benefits-for-dogs\">lick mats</a> — so the week has variety.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Shake the mat out after each use.</li>\n<li>Wash when it smells like a pantry.</li>\n<li>Keep it away from cats who will steal the kibble and leave the dog a mystery.</li>\n<li>Skip the mat if the dog has a history of eating fabric.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Puppies and seniors</h2>\n<p>Puppies need larger, easy pieces and supervision. Seniors with sore necks may prefer a raised puzzle. Adjust height and time.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/blog/dog-toys.webp\" alt=\"Dog sniffing kibble hidden in a fleece snuffle mat on the floor\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<h2>Scent games beyond the mat</h2>\n<p>Hide a few pieces in a room. That is amateur nose work. Keep it fun. Do not hide food in houseplants the dog will destroy.</p>\n<h2>Shopping a mat that can be washed</h2>\n<p>Machine-washable if possible. Browse <a href=\"/dog\">the dog aisle</a>.</p>\n<h2>Shop this at Petshiwü</h2>\n<p>Ready to restock after reading about snuffle mat? Petshiwü ships as a nationwide online pet store with free shipping over $49 and no autoship. NYC delivery is available now; nationwide shipping opens soon.</p>\n<p><a href=\"/dog\">Browse matching products at Petshiwü</a> — free shipping over $49, no autoship.</p>\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>How much food goes in a snuffle mat?</h3>\n<p>Start with a meal portion or a measured handful. If the dog finishes in 30 seconds, hide deeper or use a bigger mat.</p>\n<h3>Can snuffle mats replace a bowl forever?</h3>\n<p>Some dogs eat every meal this way. Others need a bowl for wet food. Variety is fine if calories stay honest.</p>\n<h3>Why does my dog sneeze in the mat?</h3>\n<p>Fleece dust or too-vigorous sniffing. Shake it out. If sneezing persists, ask your veterinarian.</p>\n<h2>Related Petshiwü guides</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/best-puzzle-toys-for-dogs\">Best Puzzle Toys for Dogs: Difficulty Levels That Do Not Create a Genius Criminal</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/how-much-to-feed-a-dog\">How Much to Feed a Dog: Calories, Body Condition, and the Lying Cup</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/lick-mat-benefits-for-dogs\">Lick Mat Benefits for Dogs: Calm, Baths, and a Frozen Job for the Mouth</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>This article is educational and is not a diagnosis or treatment plan. Ask your veterinarian before you change food, supplements, or medicine, and seek care right away for blood in stool or vomit, repeated vomiting, trouble breathing, collapse, or a pet that cannot keep water down.</em></p>",
