    "slug": "turtle-tank-setup",
    "title": "Turtle Tank Setup: Water Volume, Basking Dock, and a Filter That Can Keep Up",
    "description": "Turtle tank setup: gallons for sliders, a dry basking dock with UVB and heat, strong filtration, and why a 10-gallon kit is a short, dirty life.",
    "publishedAt": "2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z",
    "html": "<p>Aquatic turtles are messy, long-lived predators with a need for a dry, hot, UVB-lit dock. A 10-gallon “turtle kit” is a dirty puddle. This Petshiwü setup is water volume, filtration, and lighting. Salmonella hygiene is part of the deal — wash hands, keep turtles out of the kitchen sink.</p>\n<figure>\n  <picture><source srcset=\"/blog/reptile.webp\" type=\"image/webp\" />\n  <img src=\"/blog/reptile.jpg\" alt=\"Aquatic turtle tank with a dry basking dock, heat lamp, UVB, and a large canister filter\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" loading=\"eager\" /></picture>\n  <figcaption>Aquatic turtle tank with a dry basking dock, heat lamp, UVB, and a large canister filter</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<h2>Water they can actually swim in</h2>\n<p>A common planning phrase is 10 gallons per inch of shell as a starting conversation for sliders, with a tank that gets larger as they grow. Depth should let them flip upright. They need a filter rated for more waste than a fish-only tank of the same size. Cycle the water the same way you would a messy fish tank — <a href=\"/learning/how-to-cycle-a-fish-tank\">cycling</a>.</p>\n<p>A haul-out dock must be fully dry. Turtles with no dry land get shell and skin disease.</p>\n<h2>Basking light plus UVB</h2>\n<p>A heat lamp on the dock and a UVB source are the usual pair, similar in spirit to <a href=\"/learning/bearded-dragon-lighting-guide\">beardie lighting</a> but aimed at a dock over water. Measure dock temperature. Replace UVB on schedule. Glass lids block UV.</p>\n<p>Goldfish do not belong as feeder entertainment in a tiny shared bowl — <a href=\"/learning/goldfish-tank-size-truth\">goldfish size</a>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Use a water conditioner if your tap needs it.</li>\n<li>Do partial water changes; do not “start over” weekly unless you enjoy new-tank syndrome.</li>\n<li>Feed in a separate tub if you want the display tank cleaner.</li>\n<li>A turtle that sits in the water and never basks may be too cold, sick, or unable to climb — call an exotics vet.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Diet</h2>\n<p>Species differ. Many sliders shift toward more plant matter as they age. Commercial turtle pellets plus greens beat a goldfish-only menu. Calcium and UVB work together. Ask an exotics vet before you invent a supplement pile.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/blog/reptile.webp\" alt=\"Aquatic turtle tank with a dry basking dock, heat lamp, UVB, and a large canister filter\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<h2>Legal and lifespan</h2>\n<p>Some sliders are restricted. They can live decades. Do not buy a quarter-sized turtle for a child without a decades plan.</p>\n<h2>Shopping a real turtle system</h2>\n<p>Large tank, canister filter, dock, heat, UVB. Browse <a href=\"/reptile\">reptiles</a> and <a href=\"/fish\">fish</a> filtration.</p>\n<h2>Shop this at Petshiwü</h2>\n<p>Build the turtle tank setup shopping list in our reptile collection. Petshiwü offers free shipping over $49, no autoship, NYC delivery now, and nationwide shipping opening soon.</p>\n<p><a href=\"/reptile\">Browse matching products at Petshiwü</a> — free shipping over $49, no autoship.</p>\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>How big of a tank does a red-eared slider need?</h3>\n<p>Much larger than a 10-gallon kit. Plan for growth and strong filtration. When in doubt, go bigger.</p>\n<h3>Do turtles need UVB if they eat pellets?</h3>\n<p>Yes. UVB helps them use calcium. Pellets are not a sunlight substitute.</p>\n<h3>Why does the tank always smell?</h3>\n<p>Underfiltration, overfeeding, and not enough water changes. Turtles are messy. Size up the filter and the water.</p>\n<h2>Related Petshiwü guides</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/how-to-cycle-a-fish-tank\">How to Cycle a Fish Tank: Bacteria, Test Kits, and Why “Just Add Fish” Fails</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/bearded-dragon-lighting-guide\">Bearded Dragon Lighting Guide: UVB, Heat, and the Gradient That Makes Vitamin D</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/learning/goldfish-tank-size-truth\">Goldfish Tank Size Truth: Why a Bowl Is a Myth and Filters Are Not Optional</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>This article is educational and is not a diagnosis or treatment plan. Ask your veterinarian before you change food, supplements, or medicine, and seek care right away for blood in stool or vomit, repeated vomiting, trouble breathing, collapse, or a pet that cannot keep water down.</em></p>",
